Answer with the first Exif item in the file instead of the one describing the primary image.

Which Exif belongs to which image is stated ONLY by the `cdsc` reference in `iref`. The failure
this control proves a test can see is silent and wrong rather than absent — a memo dated from the
decoy item, or from a secondary image whose metadata libheif does not even offer for the primary —
so the probes it must turn red are the four-item fixture's capture date and the lone-secondary
fixture, and nothing else.

--- a/app/services/capture.py
+++ b/app/services/capture.py
@@ -405,6 +405,7 @@ def _heif_exif_item(meta: bytes, children: dict[bytes, tuple[int, int]]) -> int
     iref = children.get(b"iref")
     if not items or primary is None or iref is None:
         return None
+    return items[0]
     body, end = iref
     if body + 4 > end or meta[body] > 1:
         return None
